def iter_outbox(root): ...
def extract_events_from_text(text): reuse logic? I'd rather import research_map/comms.py's _json_objects but that module has side effects (constants only) — importing is fine: sys.path.insert(research_map); from comms import _json_objects. But comms.py ROOT is computed from __file__, fine. Importing comms also imports schemas. That's acceptable. But careful: comms module name might clash; use importlib with explicit path. Simpler: implement a local light parser mirroring jsonl/json/fenced. Since our outbox files are pure jsonl from us and peers, a line-based parser + whole-file JSON is enough. But flash-15 wrote pure jsonl; w06 pure jsonl; there may be .md with fenced blocks. I'll implement a small parser (whole-file JSON, then lines).

def probe(root):
  findings = {"artifact_path_collisions": [], "duplicate_proposals": [], "class_leakage": [], "malformed_events": [], "rejected_events": []}
  map_ = json.load(map path)
